    "description": "FlutterBlocFirebaseClean Architecture\n\nLocation\n\nMohan Estate, New Delhi\n\nEmployment Type\n\nFull time\n\nLocation Type\n\nOn site\n\nInterview Process\n\n1\n\nApplication Review\n\n2\n\nScreening Round\n\n3\n\nCoding Round\n\n4\n\nAI Interview Round\n\n### **About Nikah Forever**\n\nNikahForever is India\u2019s leading Community Matrimony platform, dedicated to making marriages simple and accessible. With a mission to foster a stronger community, we have proudly facilitated 70,000+ successful matches and served over 2 million members. By leveraging AI-based algorithms, we streamline the process of searching and connecting with compatible profiles. Our platform redefines how people perceive and approach marriage, ensuring an easy and efficient experience.\n\n### **Responsibility**\n\nRole Overview\n\nJob Title: SDE-1 (Mobile Application) Experience\n\n* 6 months \u2013 1 year of software development experience.\n* Freshers with exceptional projects may also be considered.\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\n* Develop and maintain mobile applications for Android and iOS..\n* Build new product features from requirement to deployment..\n* Integrate REST APIs and backend services..\n* Debug, optimize, and improve application performance..\n* Collaborate with backend, product, and design teams..\n* Write clean, maintainable, and scalable code..\n* Participate in code reviews and engineering discussions..\n* Learn new technologies and contribute to improving development processes..\n\nWe're Looking For Someone Who\n\n* Has experience in software development (backend or frontend)..\n* Wants to build a long-term career in mobile application development..\n* Has good programming fundamentals and problem-solving skills..\n* Understands APIs, JSON, HTTP requests, and client-server architecture..\n* Has basic knowledge of Git and version control..\n* Is eager to learn new technologies quickly..\n* Can work independently while collaborating effectively with a team..\n* Pays attention to code quality and user experience..\n\nPreferred Skills\n\nExperience in any of the following is a plus: \u2022 Flutter. \u2022 Android (Java/Kotlin). \u2022 iOS (Swift). \u2022 React Native. \u2022 JavaScript / TypeScript. \u2022 Node.js. \u2022 Python. \u2022 MySQL or PostgreSQL. \u2022 Firebase. \u2022 REST APIs.\n\nNote: Prior Flutter experience is not mandatory. We value strong engineering fundamentals and the willingness to learn.\n\nWhat You'll Learn\n\nYou'll get hands-on experience with: \u2022 Cross-platform mobile development. \u2022 Flutter ecosystem. \u2022 Large-scale backend integration. \u2022 State management. \u2022 App architecture and clean coding practices. \u2022 Performance optimization. \u2022 CI/CD and release management. \u2022 Analytics, crash reporting, and debugging. \u2022 AI-assisted software development.\n\nIdeal Candidate\n\nYou enjoy solving real-world problems, learning new technologies, and building products used by thousands of users. You're curious, proactive, and excited about growing into a well-rounded software engineer.\n\nWhy Join Us?\n\n* Work on a real-world product with a large active user base..\n* Learn directly from experienced engineers..\n* Opportunity to work across mobile and backend technologies..\n* Ownership of features from idea to production..\n* Fast learning environment with continuous growth..\n* Exposure to scalable systems and modern engineering practices..\n\nLocation\n\nOn-site\n\n### **Qualification**\n\n* A few months of Flutter development experience through projects or internships is preferable\n* Experience working in a product-based company is preferred\n* Strong understanding of Flutter widgets and rendering\n* Hands-on experience with state management using BLOC and Provider (mandatory)\n* Understanding of navigation, dependency injection, and application lifecycle\n* Experience working with REST APIs and JSON\n* Familiarity with Firebase (RTDB, Authentication, Crashlytics, FCM)\n* Knowledge of app performance optimization techniques\n* Solid experience with Git and GitHub workflows, including pull requests, code reviews, and branching strategies\n* Familiarity with Flutter, Dart, GetX, and Provider\n* Experience using AI coding tools such as GitHub Copilot, Cursor, or similar AI-powered IDEs\n* Knowledge of CI/CD tools such as Fastlane and GitHub Actions is a plus\n* Experience with Play Store and App Store deployments is a plus\n* Strong ownership mindset with the ability to ship features independently\n* Product-oriented thinking with a focus on user experience, performance, and stability\n* Proactive approach to identifying and suggesting improvements\n* Comfortable working in a fast-moving startup environment\n* Ability to use AI tools effectively and responsibly to improve development efficiency",
